<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Trading quiet after hours.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Trading quiet after hours.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>After-hours trading was quiet, due to little corporate news and the Yom Kippur holiday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very quiet. Everyone took the opportunity to skirt on home today. There's nothing going on,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>After hours, Hartford Steam Boiler Inspection &amp; Insurance Co said it expects to take storm-related charges of $0.25-$0.30 a share in the third quarter and IMP Inc said it expects to record a significant loss in the second quarter ended September, due to weaker demand and restructuring charges.</p>
</text>
